course: dictionary
lesson: 14376
title: Words that tell us what usually happens
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us how often something happens, or how things are normally done. Ordinarily is one of them. The words around it leave clues. «Ordinarily, I walk to school.» The word ordinarily tells you this is what I usually do, not just today.
explain: «Ordinarily the bus is on time, but today it is late.» The word but is a clue. It tells you the bus is usually on time, and today is different. So ordinarily means usually, in the normal way.
explain: Ordinarily can also mean in an ordinary, not special, way. «The room was ordinarily furnished, with plain chairs and a table.» Nothing was fancy. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Ordinarily means usually, or in the normal way.
fact: «Ordinarily» often comes before a sentence that shows something different happened: «Ordinarily the shop opens at nine, but today it opens at ten.»
fact: In everyday talk, «ordinarily» tells you what normally happens. In formal writing, it can mean «as a rule».
fact: Ordinarily can also mean in an ordinary, not special, way.
fact: A good check is to swap in usually: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
exercise: «Ordinarily, I walk to school.» What does ordinarily mean here? | Never, not once | Very quickly | *Usually, in the normal way | Only on Sundays
exercise: «Ordinarily the bus is on time, but today it is late.» Which word tells you that today is different from the usual? | time | *but | bus | late
exercise: «The room was ordinarily furnished, with plain chairs and a table.» What does ordinarily suggest? | *In a plain, not special, way | Very slowly | Only once | In a grand and fancy way
test: «Ordinarily Mum drives me to football, but on Tuesday I cycled.» What does ordinarily mean? | Quietly | Never | *Usually, as a normal thing | Angrily
test: «Ordinarily the library is quiet, but today there is a noisy band.» Why is the word but used? | To show that the library is always noisy | To add a list of things | *To show that today is different from usual | To show that the band is quiet
exam: Which sentence means the same as «as a rule»? | «He ran ordinarily fast.» | *«Ordinarily we eat dinner at six.» | «The shop was ordinarily plain.»
